## Before class

1. **Malte Ubl — [*Design Docs at Google*](https://www.industrialempathy.com/posts/design-docs-at-google/)** — **the primary reading.** The anatomy of a design doc (context and scope, goals and **non-goals**, the design itself, **alternatives considered**, cross-cutting concerns), why the trade-offs are the whole point, and when *not* to write one at all. Read it with two things in mind, because we'll take both up in class: it describes one company's culture, where design docs are informal working documents — that is not true everywhere — and "alternatives considered" can rest on anything from a hallway conversation to weeks of measured work. *(Heads-up: one embedded meme in the "The actual design" section has profanity in its caption. The point it makes is a fair one; the rest of the article is clean.)*
