## What you'll leave with

- **A read on the genre's quality bar** — from a document you critiqued rather than a description you were given.
- **Your project's skeleton on paper**, ready for Wednesday's whiteboard workshop.
- **The <course-link type="page" id="pg-design-doc-template">design document template</course-link>**, which is the required structure for <course-link type="assignment" id="cp5">CP5</course-link> — download the Markdown and it becomes `docs/design.md` in your repo. Organizations standardize these so reviewers always know where to look; conforming to one is part of the job.
